 "input": "AfD in practice: editor thinks an article isn't notable. should do a search first (WP:BEFORE) to check for sources. then tag the article with the AfD template and create the discussion page, and it gets listed on the daily log. notify the article's creator on their talk page. other editors comment keep/delete citing policy (notability guidelines mainly). runs 7 days. then an uninvolved admin or experienced editor closes it, reading consensus not counting votes. if delete, admin deletes the article. people can go to deletion review if they think the close was wrong.",
